    31	- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
    32	- **The rule on the tenth, in Oryn's hand and his:** *ask first, every time.* It was paid once, by not reading Teague.
    33	- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
    34	- **Brom:** right shoulder bolted on the Stair and mended, reopened in the Hall and mended a second time ("Twice… not three times this season"). Then bound by Teague's healer of no Path and carried guarded. Carries the kit and the middle box.
    35	- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
    36	- **Seln:** unmarked all book. The case carried, unopened, targeted, kept. Angry once (the Stair's rim: "No faces." and a broken stock).
    37	- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route, **three weeks late there** and the route whole. Letter: "Six, by letter." She learned the mechanism on the 100th. She has not heard any theory, because there is none.
    38	- **Who knows the mechanism:** six (Oryn added). Teague, Pike, the holds and the faceless faction do not.
    39	- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
    40	- **Teague:** "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) stays at Lowmarch through the cold term. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the cold term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch24 — OWNER-pending #48]
    41	- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
    42	- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
    43	- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **about four hundred and forty yards' radius** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
    44	- **The Compact:** knows quiet ground exists and what it does, and which crew walks out of it (a completion report on the Fallow contract; the rim on the Stair saw a practitioner walk out *declaring*). **It does not know that anything works inside.** Asset-restriction is still pending. The nameless second Anchor hand: "the account's getting longer."
    45	- **Letters west on the last ferry:** to Hesk ("Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof…") and to Vell ("There's a second ledger on the continent…").
    46	- **Last paragraph:** verbatim (§10, Ch24).
