editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-153-### 5.2 Learning and training arcs (effort into capability)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-154-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md:155:- **Compression apprenticeship** (M1–M5): road sessions continue (quarter of a slow push, clumsy, costly) → half a push (M2) → full slow push and a first fast catch (M4) → hardened enough to survive one deliberate crossing of a heat channel in the match, at the price of a forearm burn (M5). Each step has a cost the reader can feel (shoulder and sternum toll; the knee mis-route once).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-156-- **The Iron read refined** (M1–M5): through three grades of cloth (M3–M4 sessions), eyes closed at D1, then — in the null sessions at three paces — a faint density where her points are about to bloom. In the match it gives him her points "as pressure before they were light."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-157-- **Wind framework under constraint** (M1, M3, M5): panel speed; anticipation scales with the opponent's body, thins against faster opponents; spent hard in the match; two misfires afterward.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-158-- **The Ember apprenticeship begins** (M6, M8): only after three clean days. Contact only, one point, his own hand. It is not what he expects; Karis rewords what he took twice in Book 3 (Book 4 says the understanding took two months and three rewordings — the third and the "decision point" understanding belong to the off-page final term). The cost is real and invisible to watchers.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/BOOK_MAP.md-159-- **Registry law as a training floor** (M6–M7): reading in enactment order; amendments as confessions; scars where the code learned fear; the wrong road; the definitions clause; the schedule walked whole. Karis reads the schedule with him on evenings in the final ten days as an independent second reader (this makes Book 4 Ch22 true).
--
