editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-654-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-655-**Abilities.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-656-- **Wind-adjacent.** Spent hard in the match. Two half-second *absences* (not slowness) at Friday dawn, about 18 hours after: the third and eleventh sequences. Clean Saturday, Sunday and Monday (Monday at three-quarter speed, a double included). Lead a quarter of a breath, unchanged (Karis counted).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md:657:- **Iron-adjacent.** In the match it gave her near points as pressure about half a breath before light, within close range (the quiet-room three paces). She answered by laying far points outside its range. Clean on Brom on the Friday. Post work at four in twenty (wk14 and wk16).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-658-- **Pressure-adjacent.** Unused; untested after the match ("no honest way to test it without a fight").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-659-- **Compression-adjacent.** New: **the fast drop.** The fragment is woken before the strike, a quarter is caught and let go unsent. Two of three. Cost: one breath and a strap across the breastbone. "The cost lives in the sending, not the catching." It takes force, never heat. Used once in the match to cross a lit Drawn Channel: it dropped the channel's shove, and the heat burned the forearm by his choice. After the match, a slow quarter at half weight, dropped, was clean.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md-660-- **Ember-adjacent.** **ACQUIRED** in the match's third exchange; the notice is P1 verbatim (ch36). It was lit once at the moment of taking, a rough point under the right palm on the frozen earth, the size not chosen. It sits warm, untested, and "feels like her." Lira's rule permits a first small touch from Tuesday of wk17, with somebody in the room.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-164-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-165-She held the point she was holding and did not look round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-166-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md:167:"Before your points light. At three paces. I think the read picks up the place they're going to be. A thickening, where it'll bloom, before it blooms." He made himself say it exactly. "Three times in about a dozen. Not every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-168-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-169-She let the point go on its count, and the shimmer of it hung a long time in the air, because she was very tired now. Then she bent and wrote, slowly, and her hand was not quite steady. She wrote it in his words, and read it back to him, and he listened and changed nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-170-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-192-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-193-That evening Karis read the ledger back to him in the archive, at Prynn's long table. She read all fourteen sessions in order, as the fourth clause said she must before any of it existed anywhere else.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-194-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md:195:She read it in her flat even voice, the voice she used for timings, and he listened to fourteen sessions of his own failure set down in another person's handwriting. *Distance nine paces. Distance one. Source's back turned. Declarations unannounced. Source tired. Witness eating. Witness withholding pen. Duration three hours and some minutes.* And after every one of them, the same word, written the same size, with the same care.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-196-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-197-*Null.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-28.md-198-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-14-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-15-Compression-adjacent was Reydan's, and he did not need to make himself remember that one, because he remembered it every time he breathed deep. Six hundred people. An Iron Rank Eight across the chalk. Everything he had built in Ardenmere riding on the fourth exchange, and the fourth exchange going wrong, and the thing arriving so late that a moment more would have made it useless to him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-16-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md:17:He laid the four of them side by side on the page, and then he laid Karis beside them: fourteen sessions in a whitewashed room, nine paces and five and one, a quarter-hour and three hours, every one at demonstration intensity, with consent given aloud, and a rule at the bottom of the page that ended everything the moment anything happened she had not chosen. Nothing in that room had ever been used against him. Nothing in it had been trying. Nothing in it had cost anything if he failed except a line in a ledger that said *null*, which Karis was glad to write.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-18-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-19-Four moments with something real riding on them, and fourteen with nothing riding on anything, and the four were the ones that had paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-29.md-20-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-140-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-141-He saw her see it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-142-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md:143:It was a single small flicker across her face, there and gone, the researcher in her noting a reading that did not fit, at the speed of a fight. She did not stop or hesitate. She changed. The next three points did not go down near him at all; they went down far off, at the edges of the ring, four and five and six paces from him, well beyond where any read could feel the air lean. She had worked out from the way he moved that he could feel her points coming when they were close, and in the space of two steps she had moved her whole floor out to where he could not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-144-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-145-Then she joined them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-146-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md:147:A channel ran across the ring from one far point to another, seven paces long, singing, and swept the floor between them in half, and another lit beside it. The far points needed no reading once they were lit; he could see them as well as anyone on the benches. They were boxing the middle of the ring into narrower and narrower lanes. Inside the lanes her near points still bloomed close, and the read still gave him those half a breath early, but the long lines were coming from where he could not feel.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-148-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-149-He was being herded, and he could see where. She was walking him toward the east chalk, into a corner made of three long channels and two short ones, and once he was in it the halt would be called as it had been called the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-150-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-168-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-169-He reached for her breastbone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-170-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md:171:It was one honest reach, the open palm he had laid on Edran's chest, and for the first time in the match she gave ground. She went back a full step, fast, and then another, and he saw the whole floor convulse round its maker. Her near points went out in a rush of shimmer and two long channels died, released, while she laid new points as she went back, three of them, in a tight curve behind her, three paces off.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-172-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-173-His hand closed on cold air a finger's width from her coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-174-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md:175:The new points joined. A short channel ran between him and her, low and bright, and another beside it, and he was standing in her middle distance with a line of fire on either side of him and her three paces away, and nothing to do there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-176-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-36.md-177-"Halt," said Wray. "Position."
