editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-15.md:189:The channels lit all at once. Thin lines of heat ran along the chalked earth from point to point to point, faintly glowing, with a sound like a kettle a moment before it sings. They did not run everywhere. They ran exactly where she had wanted them. In the space of a single breath, a ring that had looked open a moment before became a drawing of a ring, lines across it in every direction a body might want to go, and between the lines, Cael saw, there were only two places left where a person could stand without crossing one. She was already moving toward one of them. The other was three paces to Edran's right, and to reach it he would have to step across a channel.
