    29	There were three ribs. He knew the number without touching them; he had heard it. They were low on the left side, and they let him breathe in to a certain depth and then they stopped him, quite firmly, as a hand stops a door. The calf had opened along the line of the old bite. Seln had taken off his own neckcloth and bound it, and the cloth was already dark.
