    31	- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
    32	- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch10 — OWNER-pending #48]
    33	- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
    34	- **Six over; the site catalogued** (eleven uprights broken at eleven heights; floor twenty-six strides; level under the cord; seamless under his palms, written only as "no seam"; the lip; Karis's chips don't match; the bands "None I own…"). **No instruments anywhere.** **The den** under the far lip (fresh prints; bones in one clause; scat; a hollow worn smooth). "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." Everyone looks at the line and the sun, then at Oryn, then at him. The log at the far lip (protected).
    35	
    36	## What must remain true / withheld
    37	
    38	- Only the two private tests, unwitnessed, never logged as deployment. Shadow untouched. Nobody sees him do anything.
    39	- The word *Quieting* does not exist yet. Say "the line", "quiet ground", "inside". "Made" is said once, by Karis.
    40	- "Compact" is not said aloud: the stake is the "registry stamp." Seln's map memory is M5's.
    41	- Oryn reads nobody inside. She has now crossed (with Brom and with the six); her eight solo crossings are M5's.
    42	- No stillhound is seen; it is all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
    43	- Ephram's letter carries "Bracken" (he). Vell's carries "The session still stands," unexplained.
    44	
    45	## What the author owns
    46	
    47	The six-day road's incidents; the plank and the room; how the letters land; the void road's country; Thornwater's evening; the order and texture of the trials; the site's light; Teague's and Karis's windows.
    48	
    49	## Where we leave pressure
    50	
    51	Day 96, the sun on the ridge and going: six people a hundred and fifty yards inside a perfect circle, at the far lip of a den. The middle box is on Brom's back and the healer's hands don't work. The stone is two hundred and twenty yards west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] One of them has told nobody that nothing happened to him.
