editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:129:**Physical challenge or learning encounter per movement:** M1 the wash recovery, the hold drilled, the Thornwater stretch walked at dusk · M2 the ford (developed fight), the well, Lira's first runs on a stiff ankle · M3 the fan haul, the bench, the stampede (terrain fight), the lip · M4 the perimeter walk and the six trials inside the line (a learning encounter for every one of the six) · M5 the Ring (central set piece), the deep reading · M6 **the deliberate quieter movement:** the bowman's one-armed shooting lessons, Cael relearning the Wind economy in Thornwater's yard under the listening, and the strata demonstration · M7 the run to the stair, the stalemate, the ascent and the rim · M8 the wyrm trials and the Hall, then the walk home into first snow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:214:| M5 | The deep reading (twenty minutes, at contact) | 4,000–4,500 | Keystone learning encounter |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:313:- Ch16: Lira: "You told me when you knew. You don't know. So you told me *that*. Keep doing it." … "It scares you." / "Out there I was the thing the system couldn't hold." … "In there I was the only thing that *worked*. I don't know which one's worse." / "The second one. You're allowed to say so." — Seln: "They know something turns Paths off. They *don't* know something doesn't turn off. Yet." — Oryn: "My hands stop at that line. Yours don't. I had my hands in you for twenty minutes and I can tell you what I didn't find, which is a Path. That's all I've got." … "I'm not going to guess past it." — Karis: "We find the others. All of them. And we find out whether they're the same." … "That's how you find a handful. One at a time, for money." — Oryn: "Don't go in without me. Not because I'm any use inside. Because somebody should be outside the line who can put an arm back on." — Brom: "That's not comfort," … "I don't do that. It's a count. You like counts." — Oryn: "Once is a morning." … "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:42:- **The ford at dusk, ≈5,000, a learning fight:** the point; the river stands up on three sides; the pommel struck; every head but one. Brom declares Iron Skin, every head turns, he drops it like a coat, "He was still large," and the current takes the hound's hindquarters. Lira runs without a burst and is fast; the ankle goes all the way on the gravel; "I'm fine." **The pack learns** and stops testing silent bodies. Karis holds the knife by its blade with both hands rather than light a second point. **The seam:** they follow the first mover, not a leader, and the grey at the bar's tip is waiting. **One Wind burst, spent openly**, downstream and away from Karis: the landing lock with a dog in it. Seln rises out of the pool behind the grey. Five dead; **two gone downstream, logged as open.** Give the opponent its learning, and keep each decisive exchange in physical terms.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:26:- **Six days Oxhollow → Lowmarch (days 84–90), lightly on the page:** the ford walked quiet a day behind Teague's crew; Lira's carter's boot for two marks, packed with linen; the tape hated by noon; Brom keeps the healer's week to the hour and picks up the middle box with both hands on the eighth morning. A small physical problem on the road is optional and the author's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45:- **Oxhollow (day 84):** the table under the lean-to, hers twenty days at a time; worst first; "That's three." The map paid seventy ("Then they go round."). **The second and third readings** (ribs knitting with "nothing doing it"; the wrist and neck, nothing wrong, still nothing): "a river in the dark." **The two readings taught before they are load-bearing** (surface: a count of ten; deep: both hands, minutes, still and whole, at a mending's cost; "I don't run it on a road"). If the stall is named (C8 default: at most once), it is a limit she prices and hates, never used. **Three questions** (right places — yes; faster; no healer ever got anything — no). "That's the visit." He has a sentence asking her south and does not say it. "Thornwater's on my route in nine days… I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:51:- Oryn knows nothing of fragments; no deep reading is run. She records nothing and remembers. Her Tide in full: contact only; about three serious mendings a day, fed and slept (two on a road); cannot heal herself; "cannot mend what I can't read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:29:- **Day 100, the deep reading (≈4,500):** the back room fixed from the door (window, table, stool, the roll in her order); "Breathe like a man asleep."; the count of ten ("Nothing. As before."); then the long one. The current goes *along*, not down; she can be felt keeping time; her commentary on banks (Iron Skin walled, Ember hot, Wind too fast to feel), "there's more water"; Shadow draws in under her touch; Storm quiet; he understands she is not afraid of him, because her trade has no room for being impressed; "Eleven years…". **The conditions arrive.** He could stop it, and stopping would be the lie. *He reached. Directed. Open-eyed. Still.* **The notice, exactly.** Two firsts counted; the third not written. "Something just changed…" / "No. I did. I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:42:The fight's moment-to-moment staging inside the planted geometry; each companion's experience of being Pathless; the night's sounds; the camp's small mercies; the walk back; the loft's lantern and its oil; the sensation language of the deep reading, held to sensation and never to explanation; both windows.

codex
The draft’s core chronology and injury ledger are holding. I’ve found one definite knowledge-boundary breach: Teague is explicitly told why Oryn missed his crew, although the packet limits him to what he can read from the yard. I’m now checking the protected quotations against their full source units before deciding whether that and the power-range issue are local repairs or require a broader verdict.
