   256	
   257	"I walked five roads out of this meadow before any of you had used one, and three more out of a hold, and I lay in the grass above a river. On each evening of those fifty days I have come back and sat down, and looked up." He ran his thumb along the bark's edge. "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report."
   258	
   259	Cael said nothing for a breath.
   260	
   261	He had looked at the dust on those boots on the first night in this meadow, and had deliberately looked somewhere else, and he had gone on doing so every evening since. He had thought that he was leaving a man his mornings. He had not known that the man sat down at their fire each night braced for a level voice across a table.
   262	
   263	He knew what the voice would say, for he could hear it. *What did you see?* He had been on the other side of it himself for two years, with that same mild face writing down his answers.
   264	
