editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:225:- **The stillhound, as seen:** grey, low, long in the back, calf-high at the shoulder, head carried level; silent in grass; the frogs stop ahead of it and start behind; prints as broad as a palm.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:227:- **The carter's map (flag):** a scraped calfskin in oak-gall ink and burnt stick: roads as double lines, fords as three wavy strokes, holds as a square with a dot, Lowmarch as a ring with a bar, days as ticks, and bare hide wherever a wheel has no business. Given to Karis for the wheel Brom rebuilt. Five roads run off its edges.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:228:- **Teague, as seen (flag):** forty or so, middle height, heavy in the forearm, cropped hair grey over the ears; a black leather band laced on the right wrist; a hand-axe in his belt; a coat mended by somebody else. His week on the cold road is salt on mules to the top holds before frost shuts the pass, along two miles of ledge; he has done it nine times. He thinks only "the spear", "the bow" (a bad leg), "the boy". One other crew on the sheet could clear the ford and is up the north road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:279:- **"They stop inside, where the tiers are": "they" are HEALERS.** The protected unit's full three-speech form is on the page at the steading's gate (ch13). Lira's thought about ranks is her own inference on the road. No healer appears; "the nearest walks a route and she's not due" stands; **Lira's ankle is not mended in this book** and her run on day 65 is a chosen risk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:282:- **Bodies:** Cael bitten through the calf ("the calf in elevens"); Karis's hand cannot hold a pencil; Lira's ankle splinted, then walking; Brom's shoulder in a sling. Exact states are in the author's state section below, as corrected after repair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **Injuries, as fixed on the page:** Brom, left forearm, two furrows from wrist to mid-arm, to the bone, fourteen stitches; opened again at the wrist on day 59 (a hand put out to steady the cart in a wet rut), seen at the fire that night; stitches out on day 64; closed clean and re-wrapped on day 66. Lira, right ankle, the ligaments, bound flat to a barrel-stave; a stick from the bowman on day 56, left against the inn wall on day 64. Karis, two cuts across each palm; bound fists, then strips; a pencil on day 68. Cael, left calf, in at the outside and out at the inside; eleven strides, then twenty (day 62), then "a leg on level ground" and nine uphill (day 69).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:315:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:317:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. Right ankle: ligaments, never seen by a healer, bound eleven days; no stick since day 64; runs on the gravel bar from day 65; "it bends less, and later". No burst at the ford or since. She killed one hound with the long knife. Her question stands unanswered in Cael's log.
