+
+No day is skipped in a way that changes an injury, debt, route promise, or board state. Movement 4 can open at dusk on day 84 even though the intercut Oryn window has looked forward to day 92 (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-337`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`).
+
+## 4. Standing defaults
+
+- **PASS — calendar language.** No season name, month name, month order, or English weekday appears. Generic *season*, *cold term*, *thaw*, frost, and weather are permitted (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:189`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:35,319`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:122-125`).
+- **PASS — measures.** The edition uses feet, yards, paces, hands, fingers, miles, and ordinary counts; no metric unit appears (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:159-195`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:55-63`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:122-125`).
+- **PASS — Cael.** No year-count since Kindling is stated; references to his Kindling or age fourteen are event anchors, not elapsed-year arithmetic (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:151`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:323-329`). He remains eighteen, and the word *nineteen* is withheld (`STATE_LEDGER.md:315`; `BOOK_MAP.md:19,31`). Narration never says “his Path” or “Cael's Path”; it says fragments, the nine, or the dark assessment history (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:5`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-149`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:126-130`).
+- **PASS — Reader Standard.** Concrete action precedes explanation, technical terms are defined in scene, and the measured prose remains accessible; the potentially abstract Tide lesson is grounded in leg, wrist, ribs, hands, and a ten-count (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:197-257`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89`).
+- **PASS — injury wording.** “The calf was a leg again” means Cael can use it on level ground; it does not claim Tide mending (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:3-5`). The leg that Oryn mends is Lira's tibia, while her ankle remains unmended and Cael's reopened calf receives cloth only (`BOOK_MAP.md:222,358`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:197-245,317-357`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:157-211`).
+
+## 5. Protected text
+
+Every BOOK_MAP-protected unit assigned to source chapters 5–7 appears once in the movement. Speaker attributions are sometimes restaged, which §10 expressly permits (`BOOK_MAP.md:238-240`). No protected document is printed twice.
+
+- **Source Ch5 units — PASS.** Pike's rule is exact once (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-05.md:107`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:19`); “landslide with legs” is exact once (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-05.md:171-183`; `manuscript/chapter-17.md:237-251`); the complete protected close is exact once and stands as one paragraph (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-05.md:243-245`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:205`).
+- **Source Ch6 units — PASS except the packet's partial “Cold” unit.** Lira's three protected replies retain their order and antecedent (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-06.md:111-119`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:329-339`). Oryn's introduction, rank, “That's one,” contact/self limit, and the entire failed-reading exchange are exact once (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-06.md:171-189,203-213,241-265`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:161-189,245-257,317-351`). The day-80 log is exact once (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-06.md:233-235`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:361-369`). The author split “Cold … No. It's going along” around invented narration, although the full source unit is a single sentence whose sequence makes *it* the felt mending moving along (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-06.md:199-205`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:229-235`). Fix 3 restores that exact source sentence and changes nothing inside it.
+- **Source Ch7 units — PASS.** “A tape and a season,” the route arithmetic, the memory-book speech, the city/route want, the river image, the promised long reading, the nine-day appointment, the keeper's verdict, Teague's four lines, and the close log are each exact once (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-07.md:29-39,49-81,101-105,127-171,177-201`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:157-195,221-293,321-365`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-87,127-133,299-333`). “Then they go round” still refers to carts, and “this” to the delivered map (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:321-351`). “They always have” still refers to Cael's hurts healing on their own (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:333-351`).
+- **Packet-only quoted lines — one wording repair.** The cart rule, *floats*, *Derived. Not tested.*, two-hands request, first-light line, shelter call, cart loss, ledge/Lira order, set warning, contact/self limit, Brom's wrist diagnosis, Ember finding, *Hm*, tape, carrying/not pulling, lateness, third mending, “nothing doing it,” road refusal, and visit close are present word-for-word in their required places (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:77`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:73`; `manuscript/chapter-17.md:237,257`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:191`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:67,89,331-339`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:205,253-257,273-297`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:23,77-81,247`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:31,57,87,113`). The packet's quoted Tide axiom is only paraphrased at present (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:31-35`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:51`); fix 4 puts “cannot mend what I can't read” on the page without duplicating the later protected “I can't mend…” unit (`BOOK_MAP.md:309`).
+- **Documents — PASS.** Ch5's protected close occurs only at `chapter-18.md:205`; Ch6's day-80 log only at `chapter-20.md:363`; Ch7's close only at `chapter-22.md:333` (`BOOK_MAP.md:271-277`). The other log paragraphs are distinct entries, not duplicate printings (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:199-207`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:243-249`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:197-205`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
+
+The 2% skeleton / 22% close probe is not a finding: protected overlap is accounted for, and the expanded mountain, treatment, and windows are independently composed (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:9-10,101-103`).
+
+## 6. New canon minted
+
+Rulings follow the AUTHOR-REPORT list in order (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:105-128`).
+
+1. **KEEP — Oxhollow slip and mark.** It is internally consistent and remains with the five after the keeper marks it (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:19-49`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:345-361`).
+2. **KEEP — reason for the job.** The eight-day Lowmarch round, three-day mule report, and copper-per-wheel ford explain price without contradicting later geography (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:29-45`; `BOOK_MAP.md:68-73`).
+3. **KEEP — east-to-west route.** The lower crossing, north side-water, gorge, western descent, and Oxhollow arrival cohere (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:219-267`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:117-131,301-305`).
+4. **KEEP — smith's terms and cart gauge.** The arithmetic closes exactly at 116 in hand / six owed (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:115-159`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:7-11`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`).
+5. **KEEP — boxes displaced by hay.** This cleanly motivates taking all three and preserves the sealed reserve (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:143-153`).
+6. **KEEP — Brom's strap; KEEP the rope loss as an unpriced obligation.** The rope is last attached to the cart and falls under “everything else” lost (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:167-183`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:35-37`).
+7. **KEEP — shale-backs as seen.** This is observational texture compatible with the bible's armored, placid grazers; the party never says they carry a Path (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:3-19`; `manuscript/chapter-17.md:3-17`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:192-194`).
+8. **KEEP — Pike's two tales.** They remain explicitly hearsay and do not convert the herd's dead or mechanism into sworn fact (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:19-39`).
+9. **AMEND — derived-page day-78 annotation.** Keep the day-75 page itself; replace the “couldn't see both ends” reason with the two-cause/no-controlled-test reason in fix 5 (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:235-251`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:341-343`).
+10. **KEEP — mountain geometry.** Its fan, bench, narrowings, bay, fin, ledge, lip, descent, and road agree with every later use in this movement (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:61-251`; `manuscript/chapter-18.md:3-191`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:49-131`).
+11. **KEEP — map.** Sixty-two yes-lines and Karis's final no make sixty-three; the keeper buys the answer the map actually gives (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:193-205`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:219,321-365`).
+12. **AMEND — stampede specification.** Keep the involuntary Wind, nine points, eight seconds, heard-not-sworn falls, and twenty-five survivors; fixes 1–2 clarify what crosses the gorge and the hard channel-length limit (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:41-49,125-201`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:111-113`). Fix 5 preserves its evidentiary status.
+13. **KEEP — Karis's brass lamp.** It is established in her box and survives with the recovered box (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53`).
+14. **KEEP — Oryn's appearance and mule kit.** No exact age is stated; Cael's “perhaps ten years older” remains an estimate compatible with him being eighteen (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:315`).
+15. **AMEND — Tide as taught.** Contact, reserve, no self-healing, two readings, and the unused stall agree with the bible (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:197-301`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:39-87`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:178-182`). Fix 4 restores the packet's exact governing axiom; no other change is needed.
+16. **KEEP — tape.** Materials, five rib bands, 21-day removal, and Lira's ankle method are coherent and carried forward (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-27,157-211`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:27`).
+17. **KEEP — Brom's wrist order.** Mended on day 80; seven-day limit expires at the middle of day 87, matching Movement 4's eighth-morning pickup (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:267-277`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:37-43`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:26`).
+18. **KEEP — Oryn's route history.** Seven holds are counted but only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named; the window does not name the other five (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:221-293`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:183-233`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8,54`).
+19. **KEEP — carter's split hand.** It motivates the mountain report and Oryn's first task at Thornwater without naming a person or hold (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:355-357`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:211-215`).
+20. **KEEP — Oxhollow.** The ford, keeper, table, gate, and payment are compatible with its planned function and introduce no later-packet conflict (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:301-365`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:3-35`).
+21. **KEEP — unnamed roles.** No role receives an owner-reserved name (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:115-153`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:3-35,183-205`).
+22. **AMEND — Teague.** Keep two holds, two mules, the old hip, his deliberately timed stop, and his own failed appointment; cut Oryn's identification of the five as the cause and Teague's charge against them. Fixes 6–9 do exactly that (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:159-179,237-277`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`).
+
+The new-canon list otherwise does not contradict the universe bible, BOOK_MAP, or Movement 4 packet. The next-movement packet does not authorize changing any of these repaired rulings (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-42`).
+
+## 7. Names
+
+**PASS.** No new named person, place, or animal appears. Oxhollow, Thornwater, Lowmarch, Fenmark, Norhold, Ternhall, Ardenmere, Greyvane, and Ostrand are already-canon places; Hesk, Pike, Teague, and the five are already-canon people (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:21-35,55,239`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:43,97,257`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:329`; `BOOK_MAP.md:19-34,68-73`). The smith, ferryman's boy, keeper, gate woman, patients, Teague's three, mule, oxen, and shale-backs remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:115-153`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:3-35,159-189,237-275`). This satisfies the owner-name restriction (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8`).
+
+## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by MOVEMENT-004
+
+Movement 4 already carries the dusk-of-84 location, 116 in hand / six owed, taped ribs, bound calf, new leg, missing right boot, Oryn north, Teague south, nine days to Thornwater, and the three boxes (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`). It must additionally inherit:
+
+- The protected shale-back finding remains **derived, not tested** after an uncontrolled two-cause event; twenty-five are seen on day 81, while the missing five remain “heard, not sworn” (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:235-251`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:195-203`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:111-113,341-343`; fix 5).
+- Lira has spent one involuntary full Wind declaration on day 78 and refused the second; her tibia is mended/new and barred from running for a month, while the old ankle remains unmended and is now taped correctly by her own hands (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:255-321`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:309-313`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:157-211`).
+- Karis spent nine points/eight channels for eight seconds and is empty; on day 80 Oryn barred even a spark for one week. She could write one line on day 82 and hold the purse on day 84, but that does not release the restriction (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53,279-301`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:215-219,359-361`).
+- Brom's left wrist is mended under the day-80-to-day-87 rule: it may take what sits on it, nothing hanging from it, and he must release a pulling load. His hedging bill survives; the older ash wedge does not (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:267-277`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:37-43`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-5,35-37`).
+- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
+- Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
+- After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
+- The three boxes are whole at Oxhollow; the reserve is sealed in the third. The marked Oxhollow slip must return to Pike. The long map leaf was paid for on the keeper's board; the keeper is its buyer. Seln's closed case remains on its strap, and Hesk's satchel still carries the log, old volume, notebook, Hesk letter, and Pike's bark lines (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:153`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:27-37,89-93`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:321-361`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:323-327`).
+- The cart, ferryman's rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, flour, and ash wedge are in the gorge; the rope's replacement obligation has no price and must not silently alter the 116-in-hand / six-owed account (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:179-189`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:35-37`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`). Cael's coat has no sleeves (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:17-23`).
+- Pike's board has not yet heard the traverse: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up remain the last spoken standings until the marked slip reaches Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:174-176`). Hesk's letter is still unanswered, Lira's earlier question remains unanswered, and two stillhounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:329-331`).
