+# Verdict: REPAIR — nine local line fixes in chapters 19–22
+
+The movement's architecture, calendar, injuries, money, fragment count, and protected documents hold. Repair is required in four narrow areas: make explicit that Lira's declaration—not her body—crosses the gorge; state Drawn Channel's eight-pace join limit on Karis's road-scale lattice; restore the packet's partly quoted “Cold” unit from the source; preserve “derived, not tested” on the correct methodological ground; put the packet's Tide axiom on the page; and remove the information Oryn gives Teague beyond what Oxhollow's yard can show him (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:43-49,125-129`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:229-235`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:31-35,341-343`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:159-179,247-251`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:41,45,51-55`). No structural rewrite, reorder, new scene, or protected-document duplication is required.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+- **No closed-text contradiction in the entry state.** Chapter 14 closes with fifty-two in hand; six earned lines; Cael's calf a leg on level ground and nine strides uphill; Lira's ankle unmended; Brom shut, not sound; Karis able to hold a pencil; nine fragments held; and deployment one (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:435-451`). Chapter 15 inherits those facts without changing a number or body (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:3-7,157-163,201-207`). “No Path has been lifted by any of us since the ford” is temporally after the ford and therefore does not erase Seln's own Shadow use at the ford (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:207`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:17-25`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:275-278`).
+- **Bodies remain continuous.** Cael's old calf wound reopens and his three left-low ribs break (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:149-155`); Oryn binds but does not mend his calf because she cannot read him (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-357`). Lira's right tibia is set and mended while her older ankle is explicitly refused and taped (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:197-245`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:157-211`). Brom's left wrist reopens and is mended under a one-week restriction (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:103-117`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:267-277`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:37-43`). Karis is emptied, not injured or advanced (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53,279-301`). These states match the forward injury ledger (`BOOK_MAP.md:222`).
+- **Objects and accounts reconcile.** The three boxes and sealed reserve go onto the hired cart (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:143-153`), all three boxes are recovered (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:103-121,211-225`), and the reserve is never opened (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:27-37`). The board purse moves 52 − 6 + 70 = 116, while the lost cart creates the second six-mark obligation (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:129-159`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:347-365`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`). Seln's case remains on him and shut by inherited state; nothing opens it (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:153`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:323`). Hesk's satchel and log survive the fall (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:89-93`).
+- **The losses are determinate in the prose.** The cart, ferryman's rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, flour, and the older ash wedge were on the cart and are gone; the hedging bill survives on Brom and levers Lira's plate (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:167`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:179-189`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-5,35-37`; prior wedge: `manuscript/chapter-04.md:311-315`). The rope's ownership is known but its replacement price is not; do not invent a money figure. Cael's right coat sleeve becomes Lira's splint binding, so both sleeves are now gone (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:17-23`; prior left sleeve: `STATE_LEDGER.md:325`).
+- **Knowledge is continuous except for Teague's packet-boundary breach.** Before the fixes, Oryn tells Teague she was up a hill after a late crew and calls the five “your five”; his window then charges her missed day to them (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:165-179,247-251`). That is not knowledge read from Oxhollow's yard, contrary to the binding limit (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`) and to the window's own later claim (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:255-277`). Fixes 6–9 remove the breach. No contradiction with an earlier closed chapter otherwise survives.
+
+## 2. The movement plan and all 21 owner flags
+
+The beats occur in packet order: slip and cart (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:3-153`); fan and bench (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:219-267`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:61-251`); herd study and derived page (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:3-263`); narrowings and ledge (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3-205`); stampede (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:3-225`); fin's lee (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-139`); Oryn's arrival and hands (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-373`); lip, route, and Oxhollow (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-365`); readings, departure, windows, Teague, and log (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:3-337`). Compression and Anchor want and are refused; Shadow is unused; the mountain spends no fragment; deployment remains one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-149`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`).
+
+Owner-flag rulings:
+
+1. **KEEP — length.** 42,012 is 5.03% over the 40,000 budget, but the added room is carrying planned lip, route, table, and two-window material rather than an unplanned subplot (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:7,32-38`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:38-46`). Do not cut earned scene logic merely to hit a round estimate.
+2. **KEEP — window lengths.** Oryn's 2,098 and Teague's 1,264 are short of their approximate targets, but both windows complete their assigned functions; padding would worsen the movement overrun (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:42`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:137-233,237-295`). Fixes 6–9 narrow Teague's knowledge without requiring replacement material.
+3. **KEEP — progression vocabulary.** The strict 55/10k count understates the actual teaching: holding/refusal, derived-versus-tested method, Tide reserve/contact/readings, ranks, points, channels, and deployment are all explicit (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:43`; `manuscript/chapter-16.md:137-151,243-249`; `manuscript/chapter-17.md:199-263`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:197-301`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89`). Do not add jargon for a counter.
+4. **KEEP — derivation.** Fire and ordinary sound fail; a near strike moves only two; a frightened animal moves the whole herd without a first mover; Karis then combines that observation with the carters' use of *loud* and clearly labels the declaration claim derived (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:67-79,129-145,153-195,207-251`). She never assigns the animals a Path, consistent with the bible's “none … carry a Path” (`UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:192-194`).
+5. **AMEND — still derived after day 78.** The current “couldn't see both ends” rationale is too weak after direct observation (`manuscript/chapter-21.md:341-343`). The event was not a controlled test: the ledge failure and Wind declaration occurred in the same instant (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:37-49`). Fix 5 records two confounded causes and keeps “derived, not tested” as required (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:52`).
+6. **KEEP — fin orientation.** The fin lies square across the fall; slides bank above it and leave a lee below (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159-175`). The apex is eleven paces above its face, not a claim that the fin points downslope (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:127-145`).
+7. **KEEP — one more loud thing.** The second declaration would oppose the already-turned eastern stream and force it back across Karis's only barrier; the dam-and-bank reasoning is physical, local, and sufficient (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:139-149`).
+8. **AMEND — Karis's lattice limit.** Book 3's nine paces is the source/subject distance in a controlled session, not a stated maximum placement range (`book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-27.md:149`; `book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-25.md:233`). Do not invent a nine-pace point cap. The hard canon limit is each Drawn Channel at no more than eight paces and holding only while both endpoints hold (`book-03-no-path-given/manuscript/chapter-11.md:188-194`). Fix 2 states that every one of the eight joins obeys that limit; nine total points are below Karis's established sixteen-point maximum (`book-03-no-path-given/STATE_LEDGER.md:713-716`).
+9. **AMEND — Lira's own Wind.** The body travels about twenty feet, while the declaration and its crack cross the gorge (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:41-49,255-267`). Fix 1 makes the packet's distinction explicit; no Cael fragment is involved (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:41,50`).
+10. **KEEP — Tide stall.** It is named once, by Oryn, as a hated, unused limit at brutal two-day cost (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:39-43`). That is within C8's “at most one mention” and compatible with the bible's private lifetime count, which the prose does not disclose (`BOOK_MAP.md:357`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:178-182`).
+11. **KEEP — short/long and surface/deep.** Oryn gives colloquial and healing-house terms together, with the correct seconds/minutes, contact, stillness, wholeness, and cost distinctions (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:81-87`; `UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:178-180`).
+12. **KEEP — river, speaker, and banks.** The protected river image remains word-for-word, and attribution may be restaged (`BOOK_MAP.md:238-240,303-304`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:69-77`). The singular bed explanation teaches Tide's already-authorized flow architecture; it does not count currents, identify fragments, or say Movement 5's reserved “More than one” (`UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:178-182`; `BOOK_MAP.md:310`).
+13. **KEEP — deep-reading plant.** Four informed companions recognize that “both hands … all of me … minutes” resembles the conditions under which Cael's integrations have occurred, but nobody says so and Oryn learns nothing (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:81-91`). This foreshadows the day-100 risk without spending Oryn's “More than one” finding or telling her the mechanism (`BOOK_MAP.md:283,310,325-330`).
+14. **AMEND — Teague's cost.** A missed healer appointment is Teague's own history, but Oryn may not identify the five as its cause, and Teague may not enter that cause against them (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:165-179,247-251`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55`). Fixes 6–9 leave him only his own wait, Oryn's bare lateness, and the yard/keeper evidence (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:255-277`).
+15. **KEEP — Seln goes for help.** He walks the lip at first light; Oryn had already started because of the carter, so he neither causes nor duplicates her arrival (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:113-149,355-369`).
+16. **KEEP — twenty-five.** Cael counts twenty-five and immediately refuses to convert the missing five into five dead; the only deaths remain heard, not sworn (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:177-201`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:111-113`).
+17. **KEEP — cart-load losses.** The rope, blankets, kettle, canvas, flour, and uncarried wedge are lost with the cart (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:167`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:179-189`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:35-37`). The only priced debt remains the smith's six; the rope's replacement obligation stays open and unpriced (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`).
+18. **KEEP — boot and sleeves.** Lira's right boot remains under the plate and she reaches day 84 barefoot and taped; Cael's second sleeve becomes the splint binding (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:11-23`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:157-211`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:257-263`).
+19. **KEEP — bill and wedge.** The bill is on Brom and survives; “everything else” on the cart settles the older ash wedge as lost, rather than leaving it conditionally alive (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-5,35-37`; prior wedge: `manuscript/chapter-04.md:311-315`).
+20. **KEEP — nineteen withheld.** The word never appears in chapters 15–22; Cael remains eighteen under the governing ledger (`STATE_LEDGER.md:315`; `BOOK_MAP.md:19,31`).
+21. **KEEP — names.** No new person, place, or animal is named; see §7 (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8`; `manuscript/chapter-15.md:21-35`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:137-189`).
+
+## 3. Calendar
+
+The movement calendar is consistent with the day-69 close and the book tables (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:435-451`; `BOOK_MAP.md:68-73,122`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:7`).
+
+| Draft span | Audit |
+|---|---|
+| Day 70: slip taken; day 71: cart paid and road entered; day 72: turnoff and fan (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:3-21,157-161,201-219`) | Correct. |
+| Days 72–74: fan unload/haul, day-73 bench log, next-morning frost/herd (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:19,83-105,217-265`) | Correct. |
+| Days 74–75: first herd work and Karis's full observation day; finding dated 75 (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:31-39,97-119,235-237`) | Correct. |
+| Days 76–77: narrowings and bay; day-77 protected close (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:13,47-53,197-205`) | Correct. |
